author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The graph node floor is denominated over a population that excludes assembly-materialized placeholder nodes, so repairing a dangling reference can never lower it; The negative control for every structural floor is stated over a population the project would accept as correct, so no passing condition requires a known defect to be present; A repair that removes a meaningless edge or node is distinguishable at the gate from an erosion that removes recorded work, without a hand edit to the declaration; The graph audit's four legacy remediation codes can be executed to zero with every block-enforcement assurance gate still passing, proven by running them; Placeholder-inclusive node counts remain available as a diagnostic measurement and are explicitly marked as unsuitable as a ratchet basis"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "A structural floor is denominated over the population the project intends to preserve, so executing a prescribed repair can never fail it"
value: "Governance is only worth running if its verdict tracks the thing it claims to protect. A floor that requires broken data inverts that: the safest tracker state is the one the gate rejects."
impact: "Blocks the entire legacy graph hygiene programme: three of pm-hnc9w7's four acceptance criteria cannot be satisfied without failing a block-enforcement gate."
outcome: Node and edge floors are denominated over real recorded items and real stored edges; placeholder-inclusive counts remain a diagnostic and are never a ratchet basis.
why_now: "Demonstrated live this session, not argued: executing the audit's own prescribed remediation drove a block-enforcement gate from pass to fail."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: "Graph assembly and governance now distinguish recorded items from synthesized missing-reference placeholders, with recorded_nodes as the structural ratchet denominator."
expected_result: "Repairing a dangling reference never lowers the recorded-node floor, while deleting a real item remains detectable."
actual_result: "The live graph reports 2,467 nodes, 2,467 recorded_nodes, missing_nodes=0, zero findings, and the structural floor negative controls pass."
